# /etc/default/bluealsa — intentionally has no settings.
#
# The Debian bluealsa.service never reads this file, so daemon options set
# here are silently ignored. The real options live in the systemd drop-in
# written by scripts/build_bluealsa.sh (single source of truth):
#   /etc/systemd/system/bluealsa.service.d/10-hd-codecs.conf
#
# With the source-built bluez-alsa the a2dp-source codecs are:
# SBC (XQ), AAC, aptX, aptX-HD, LDAC. The codec is auto-selected after
# connect by scripts/bt_codec_select.sh (LDAC > aptX-HD > aptX > AAC > SBC)
# and can be switched from the web UI.
